      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Taking everything into account, this is probably a flare of bronchiectasis. Another possibility is a chest infection. A chest X-ray is what I'd like next, for bronchiectasis flare. A sputum culture is what I'd like next, for purulent sputum. I'll start you on clarithromycin, 500 milligrams, twice a day, fourteen days. It's for bronchiectasis flare. Keep up your airway clearance exercises twice a day. Let's get you seen by the respiratory clinic, I'll arrange the letter.",
